{"chapter": "sheaves", "node_kind": "proof", "parent_tag": "0094", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "\\begin{eqnarray*}\n\\Hom_{\\mathcal{O}_X}(f^*\\mathcal{G}, \\mathcal{F})\n& = &\n\\Mor_{\\textit{Mod}(\\mathcal{O}_X)}(\n\\mathcal{O}_X \\otimes_{f^{-1}\\mathcal{O}_Y} f^{-1}\\mathcal{G}, \\mathcal{F}) \\\\\n& = &\n\\Mor_{\\textit{Mod}(f^{-1}\\mathcal{O}_Y)}(\nf^{-1}\\mathcal{G}, \\mathcal{F}_{f^{-1}\\mathcal{O}_Y}) \\\\\n& = &\n\\Hom_{\\mathcal{O}_Y}(\\mathcal{G}, f_*\\mathcal{F}).\n\\end{eqnarray*}", "REF_0001": "\\ref{lemma-adjointness-tensor-restrict}", "REF_0002": "\\ref{lemma-adjoint-push-pull-modules}"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{proof}\n", "suffix": "\\end{proof}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:c90dd24351738f8846457212433dd97e0c255c7629ea737ed4595182fa6f4809", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:fd5fd0677d15d04d055c17fdf2b6f3a65552427da8eeb6c77cb5ffa045c9c68b", "source_text": "This follows from the work we did before:\n<MATH_0001>\nHere we use Lemmas <REF_0001>\nand <REF_0002>.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:47f7975ccf35a798976b5c91818e99d070dd338e9ca510b7497d6fdde2b58db7", "unit_id": "tag:0096:proof"}
{"chapter": "sheaves", "node_kind": "lemma", "parent_tag": "0094", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$f : X \\to Y$", "MATH_0002": "$g : Y \\to Z$", "MATH_0003": "$(g \\circ f)_*$", "MATH_0004": "$g_* \\circ f_*$", "MATH_0005": "$(g \\circ f)^* \\cong f^* \\circ g^*$"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{lemma}\n\\label{lemma-push-pull-composition-modules}\n", "suffix": "\\end{lemma}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:40e70ec7012fa1ba71e803cbe37f7488be0e691490661c4da5b4f0a069150ecd", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:655bb3f9c0150a4cc70165e6c7797d5b267ce3a6510d10a5347ffcece84d3867", "source_text": "Let <MATH_0001> and <MATH_0002> be morphisms of ringed spaces.\nThe functors <MATH_0003> and <MATH_0004> are equal.\nThere is a canonical isomorphism of functors\n<MATH_0005>.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:b07921e891b069a586a15fa4dd0db2e15c9996985e398a4e4de75d4704f19ede", "unit_id": "tag:0097:statement"}
{"chapter": "sheaves", "node_kind": "proof", "parent_tag": "0094", "placeholders": {"REF_0001": "\\ref{lemma-pushforward-composition}", "REF_0002": "\\ref{lemma-pullback-composition}"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{proof}\n", "suffix": "\\end{proof}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:44136fa355b3678a1146ad16f7e8649e94fb4fc21fe77e8310c060f61caaff8a", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:7a1a6efc84b6cf5a6f0512d3363b5e2a1c2c79f5d13740dfad116ef711052492", "source_text": "The result on pushforwards is a consequence of Lemma\n<REF_0001> and our definitions.\nThe result on pullbacks follows from this by the same\nargument as in the proof of Lemma <REF_0002>.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:098e33a3cebf087a9cf04529c0ebb0620fa0d60840ee2e9d72b29d4d6b213d9d", "unit_id": "tag:0097:proof"}
{"chapter": "sheaves", "node_kind": "paragraph", "parent_tag": "0094", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$(f, f^\\sharp) : (X, \\mathcal{O}_X) \\to (Y, \\mathcal{O}_Y)$", "MATH_0002": "$\\mathcal{O}_X$", "MATH_0003": "$\\mathcal{F}$", "MATH_0004": "$\\mathcal{O}_Y$", "MATH_0005": "$\\mathcal{G}$", "MATH_0006": "$Y$", "MATH_0007": "$f$", "MATH_0008": "$\\varphi : \\mathcal{G} \\to \\mathcal{F}$", "MATH_0009": "$f$", "MATH_0010": "$\\varphi : \\mathcal{G} \\to \\mathcal{F}$", "MATH_0011": "$V \\subset Y$", "MATH_0012": "$$\n\\mathcal{G}(V) \\longrightarrow \\mathcal{F}(f^{-1}V)\n$$", "MATH_0013": "$\\mathcal{O}_Y(V)$", "MATH_0014": "$\\mathcal{F}(f^{-1}V)$", "MATH_0015": "$\\mathcal{O}_Y(V)$", "MATH_0016": "$f^\\sharp_V : \\mathcal{O}_Y(V) \\to \\mathcal{O}_X(f^{-1}V)$", "MATH_0017": "$f$", "MATH_0018": "$\\mathcal{G}$", "MATH_0019": "$\\mathcal{F}$", "MATH_0020": "$\\Mor_{\\textit{Mod}(\\mathcal{O}_X)}(f^*\\mathcal{G}, \\mathcal{F})$", "MATH_0021": "$\\Mor_{\\textit{Mod}(\\mathcal{O}_Y)}(\\mathcal{G}, f_*\\mathcal{F})$", "MATH_0022": "$f$", "MATH_0023": "$f$", "MATH_0024": "$f$", "MATH_0025": "$\\mathcal{G} \\to \\mathcal{F}$", "MATH_0026": "$x \\in X$", "MATH_0027": "$$\n\\varphi_x : \\mathcal{G}_{f(x)} \\longrightarrow \\mathcal{F}_x\n$$", "MATH_0028": "$\\mathcal{O}_{Y, f(x)}$", "MATH_0029": "$\\mathcal{O}_{Y, f(x)}$", "MATH_0030": "$\\mathcal{F}_x$", "MATH_0031": "$\\mathcal{O}_{X, x}$", "MATH_0032": "$f^\\sharp_x : \\mathcal{O}_{Y, f(x)} \\to \\mathcal{O}_{X, x}$", "REF_0001": "\\ref{definition-f-map}", "REF_0002": "\\ref{lemma-f-map}", "STRUCT_0001": "\\noindent", "STRUCT_0002": "\\medskip", "STRUCT_0003": "\\noindent", "TEXTITCLOSE_0001": "}", "TEXTITOPEN_0001": "{\\it "}, "render": {"prefix": "", "suffix": ""}, "risk_level": "R2", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:69aa181fb8d1e60f65f58524d2267edcb0cac93856d0582cce4f787fabc2b233", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:53835c0f0909e695eea6b19aef0d1ab82fc5055f4a9ec462bba387574bde32b0", "source_text": "\n\n\n<STRUCT_0001>\nGiven a morphism of ringed spaces\n<MATH_0001>,\nand a sheaf of <MATH_0002>-modules <MATH_0003>,\na sheaf of <MATH_0004>-modules <MATH_0005> on <MATH_0006>,\nthe notion of an <TEXTITOPEN_0001><MATH_0007>-map <MATH_0008>\nof sheaves of modules<TEXTITCLOSE_0001> makes sense. We can just define\nit as an <MATH_0009>-map <MATH_0010>\nof abelian sheaves (see Definition <REF_0001> and\nLemma <REF_0002>) such that for all open <MATH_0011> the map\n<MATH_0012>\nis an <MATH_0013>-module map. Here we think of\n<MATH_0014> as an <MATH_0015>-module\nvia the map <MATH_0016>.\nThe set of <MATH_0017>-maps between\n<MATH_0018> and <MATH_0019> will be in canonical bijection\nwith the sets\n<MATH_0020>\nand\n<MATH_0021>.\nSee above.\n\n<STRUCT_0002><STRUCT_0003>\nComposition of <MATH_0022>-maps is defined in exactly the\nsame manner as in the case of <MATH_0023>-maps of sheaves of\nsets. In addition, given an <MATH_0024>-map <MATH_0025>\nas above, and <MATH_0026> the induced map on stalks\n<MATH_0027>\nis an <MATH_0028>-module map where the\n<MATH_0029>-module structure on <MATH_0030>\ncomes from the <MATH_0031>-module structure via\nthe map <MATH_0032>.\nHere is a related lemma.\n\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:5c65f5a615245f5e9ac389133a6191b4be00b9e6b07b184297696d87421d27ed", "unit_id": "tag:0094:prose-0003"}
